# Code owners (#470)
#
# Scope is deliberately narrow: this is not a blanket ownership map, just a
# mandatory-human-review gate on the highest-blast-radius path in the repo.
#
# tooling/manifest.py + tooling/generate_*.py are the generator core: per
# #470's own audit (`grep -rl "GENERATED by \`python -m tooling.cli
# generate\`"`), ~505 downstream files across skills/, collapsed/, and
# .claude/skills/ trace back to this module, and its own authorship (plus
# its test suite's) is concentrated in the same non-diverse contributor
# pool. The regenerate-and-diff CI gate (`auditing-architecture-conformance`)
# catches drift between this module and its generated output, but nothing
# previously required a human (as opposed to an AI-session) review of a
# change to the generator itself before merge.
#
# This only takes effect where GitHub branch protection has "Require review
# from Code Owners" enabled for the protected branch — that setting lives in
# repo Settings and isn't verifiable from this checkout (the same caveat
# #471 raises for the fork-PR gate's own GitHub Settings dependency).
/tooling/manifest.py      @brandondees
/tooling/generate_*.py    @brandondees
